marble-device-support (1.0.0-11) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Keep the sensor chain alive across SLPI restarts. hexagonrpcd exits 0 when
    its FastRPC session breaks (seen after "remoteproc0: crash detected in
    slpi", an SNS_SEE fatal error 84 s into a boot), and systemd treats a clean
    exit as success, so nothing brought it back; iio-sensor-proxy then
    segfaults on the vanished backend and Debian's unit has no Restart= either,
    leaving every sensor dead until a manual restart. hexagonrpcd now gets
    Restart=always and iio-sensor-proxy Restart=on-failure (both RestartSec=2).

