marble-device-support (1.0.0-10) unstable; urgency=medium

  * marble-imsctl apply: poll for IMS registration instead of failing on the
    first look. The boot unit runs as soon as the modem announces its QMI
    services, but the modem only registers after 81voltd has served its IMS
    PDN request, ModemManager has created the bearer and the SIP registration
    has gone through - tens of seconds later. On a cold boot the unit
    therefore exited 2 ("not registered") even though IMS came up fine
    seconds later, leaving a failed unit behind. 'apply' now retries the
    registration query every 3 s for up to 90 s; 'check' keeps its strict
    exit code for monitoring.

 -- GhfunNiHe <131235947+GhfunNiHe@users.noreply.github.com>  Thu, 15 Oct 2026 20:15:00 +0800

marble-device-support (1.0.0-9) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Enable the modem's IMS services (SMS over IMS, VoLTE) on every boot.
    The modem firmware does not register for IMS until the application
    processor says which IMS services may run - on Android ims.apk does that
    over QMI IMSS. Without it IMSA reports "not registered" (error code 0) and
    SMS keeps going out over the CS domain, which China Telecom rejects (reject
    cause 18, no 2G/3G fallback). With 81voltd hosting the IMS Data service so
    the modem can bring the "IMS" APN bearer up, marble-imsctl sends the
    "Set IMS Services Enabled Setting" message once and the modem registers by
    itself: IMSA "registered", sms/voice/video "ready", MO/MT SMS and calls
    verified on CHN-CT. The setting lives in modem NV, the boot unit only
    re-applies it for good measure. Recommends 81voltd, which is required for
    the IMS PDN.

 -- GhfunNiHe <131235947+GhfunNiHe@users.noreply.github.com>  Thu, 15 Oct 2026 19:25:00 +0800

marble-device-support (1.0.0-8) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Ship a read-only NetworkManager profile for the China Telecom data
    connection (usr/lib/NetworkManager/system-connections/ct-data.nmconnection,
    apn ctlte). NM loads /usr/lib profiles since 1.36, so a fresh rootfs has
    cellular data as a working fallback route with zero manual setup. Ships
    with autoconnect disabled: enabling it while the modem is still coming up
    races ModemManager's initialization and trips the
    mm_iface_modem_count_bearers assertion (SIGABRT, upstream master bug).
    Bring data up after registration with 'nmcli con up ct-data'.

