marble-device-support (1.0.0-7) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Power the controller back on after programming the Bluetooth address in
    marble-mac-restore.sh. The script has to power hci0 down before
    'btmgmt public-addr' can take, and bluetoothd's AutoEnable only fires
    when the index is first added - which we already raced past with the
    power off - so after a clean boot the controller sat at Powered: no even
    though the address was correct. Explicit 'btmgmt power on' closes that
    race.

