marble-device-support (1.0.0-5) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Merge marble-wlan-mac.service and marble-bt-mac.service into one
    marble-mac-restore.service: both addresses come out of the same persist
    file (qca6490/wlan_mac.bin), so one unit mounts persist once, parses the
    MAC once and has a single boot-ordering point. WLAN half keeps loading
    ath11k_pci (still blacklisted in usr/lib/modprobe.d/marble-wlan.conf);
    Bluetooth half keeps pushing the derived address (WLAN MAC minus one on
    the last octet) through btmgmt, and now only warns on failure so a
    Bluetooth problem cannot fail the unit that Wi-Fi depends on.

