marble-device-support (1.0.0-4) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Ship the Bluetooth address restore: marble-bt-mac.service derives the
    Bluetooth address from the factory WLAN MAC in persist (wlan0 minus one on
    the last octet, the Xiaomi convention seen on boards that also carry
    persist/wlan_bt/bt.mac) and pushes it through 'btmgmt public-addr'. The
    stock NV blob qca/wcnhpnv21g.bin has no BD_ADDR, so without this the
    controller reports 00:00:00:00:00:00, the kernel keeps hci0
    HCI_UNCONFIGURED and 'bluetoothctl list' is empty even though dmesg shows
    the QCA firmware download completing. The address is volatile, so this
    runs on every boot, after bluetooth.service.

